  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One worker, one truth",
      "items": [
        "the worker is the only context that holds the session, calls the SDK and writes durable state — the UI surfaces are clients that render its answers",
        "listeners are registered synchronously at the top level of the worker entry module: a listener registered after an await is a lost event",
        "Chrome terminates the worker when it is idle, so no state may live in a module global; state is rebuilt from storage on every wake"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The page is hostile",
      "items": [
        "a content script runs in the page's DOM but in an isolated world: it may capture typed data but never the SDK, the session or a token",
        "the bridge to the main world validates event.source, the origin, the payload schema and a nonce before anything is forwarded",
        "the manifest and the CSP forbid remote code: no eval, no new Function, no remote script"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The kit that ships the contract",
      "items": [
        "extension-best-practices carries the architecture contract, the messaging rules, the storage rules and the permission discipline",
        "extension-review turns the contract into a prioritized report: a broken layer wall or a missing sender check is a Must fix",
        "extension-port moves MV2 background pages, Firefox builds and web apps onto MV3 with the same behavior, porting the tests first"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The machine-checkable half",
      "items": [
        "lints/eslint.config.mjs pins the layer walls: no chrome in domain/application, no SDK in the UI, no SDK or session in content, no chrome or React in the SDK",
        "scripts/check-lints.sh proves every pinned rule fires against a planted violation, and the clean file must stay clean",
        "CI runs check, lints, examples and the unittest suite; a rule that needs an exception has not finished"
      ]
    }
  ]
